From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hayaksi1 <193020925+hayaksi1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:34:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Record the header search button the snapshots never learned
 about

The fork adds a search button to the room header and a search bar above the
timeline, and updated the two snapshots that render them. Both updates were
lost in the merge and the committed files came through byte-identical to
upstream, which left RoomView and RoomHeader failing on a tree where nothing
about the components themselves was wrong.

This class hides from a line-set comparison: a snapshot's added lines are
markup fragments that recur elsewhere in the same file, so every added line is
still found and the file reads as intact. Comparing the blob against upstream
is what catches it.
